      "wiki_content": "A Reality Tour is a live album by David Bowie released in 2010. The album features the two-night concert in Dublin during the Reality Tour in 2003. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/David+Bowie/A+Reality+Tour\">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.",
      "wiki_summary": "A Reality Tour is a live album by David Bowie released in 2010. The album features the two-night concert in Dublin during the Reality Tour in 2003. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/David+Bowie/A+Reality+Tour\">Read more on Last.fm</a>."
    },
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "A Reality Tour is David Bowie’s live album documenting performances from 22 and 23 November 2003 in Dublin, recorded during his worldwide Reality tour and released in 2010 on ISO Records and Columbia Music Video. It captures Bowie in strong late-career form, drawing on songs from across his catalog while presenting the tour as a career-spanning showcase rather than a document of a single album cycle.\n\nMusically, the set leans into rock with a broad, greatest-hits feel: songs like “Rebel Rebel,” “Fame,” “Changes,” “Life on Mars?,” and “Heroes” sit alongside deeper cuts and material from Reality, giving the release both fan-service appeal and historical weight. As an audio counterpart to the concert film, it adds bonus tracks and has been praised for its expansive, well-paced set list, which reflects the scale and ambition of Bowie’s final major world tour.",
      "generated_at": "2026-08-09T14:09:43.513090",
